<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Valentinian III</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">419–455</span> · Also known as Flavius Placidus Valentinianus</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Valentinian III was Western Roman emperor from 425 to 455, placed on the throne as a child with the support of the Eastern court and ruled at first under the regency of his mother Galla Placidia. His reign saw the loss of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/africa">Africa</a> to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vandals">Vandals</a> and the invasions of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/attila">Attila</a>, while real power lay with the general <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/flavius-aetius">Aetius</a>. Valentinian murdered Aetius in 454 and was himself killed by Aetius's followers in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> in 455.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/valentinian-iii.jpg" alt="Valentinian III" width="320" height="373" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Tony Querrec (photo) · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bust_of_Valentinian_III,_Louvre_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
